content.text:
Now re-test mobile portrait and desktop layout. Also I should double-check the desktop stage: with stage width min(100%, 100dvh*16/9) and stage-wrap flex:1 with padding, height fits. At 1440x900: stage width min(1440, 1600)=1440, aspect 16/9 → height 810, stage-wrap height 900-12=888 → fits with 39px top/bottom. Good.

At 1280x720: stage width min(1280, 1280)=1280 → height 720; wrap height 708 (padding 6) → max-height 100% clamps height to 708? CSS max-height:100% with aspect-ratio and width 1280 → height 720 > 708 → height clamps to 708 but width stays 1280? With aspect-ratio, if height is constrained, width should shrink? For a replaced-like element with aspect-ratio and max-height, the width may remain 1280 and height 708 → distorted. Hmm. Canvas CSS width/height 100% would then stretch.

Safer: keep width calc based on available height. We can use `max-width: calc(100dvh * 16 / 9)` on #stage plus `width:100%`. Then at 720 height: max-width = 1280 → width 1280, height 720; wrap height 708 → still overflow 12px.

Since stage-wrap has padding 6px top/bottom, available height = 100dvh - 12. Use `max-width: calc((100dvh - 12px) * 16 / 9)`. At 720 → 1258 wide, 708 high. Good. On desktop 900 → (888)*16/9=1578 → width 1440 → 810 high < 888. Fine.

But in the touch media, stage-wrap is auto height and touch takes the rest; the stage width 100% → height 219 on 390. The max-width based on 100dvh doesn't matter (1500). Good.

Set `max-width: calc((100dvh - 12px) * 16 / 9)`.

Hmm with mobile browser dynamic viewport, 100dvh handles it.

Let me update #stage width/max-width:
```css
#stage {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: calc((100dvh - 12px) * 16 / 9);
  aspect-ratio: 16/9;
  max-height: 100%;
}
```
And stage-wrap centers.

On portrait touch layout, stage-wrap has padding 6px+; width 100% (390-12=378) → height 212.6. Good.

